---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Flash an ELF or raw .bin image to the target

Usage: pogo flash [OPTIONS] <IMAGE>

Arguments:
  <IMAGE>
          ELF (preferred) or raw .bin image

Options:
      --address <ADDR>
          Flash address for a raw .bin, e.g. 0x10000

      --chip <CHIP>
          Chip type [default: auto-detect]

      --flash-baud <BAUD>
          Baud rate used while flashing

      --bootloader <BIN>
          Custom bootloader image

      --partition-table <CSV|BIN>
          Custom partition table

      --no-verify
          Skip read-back verification

      --no-reset
          Stay in the bootloader after flashing

      --erase-all
          Erase the entire flash first (guarded; requires --confirm)

      --confirm <USB_SERIAL>
          USB serial of the device, confirming --erase-all

      --allow-bootloader-write
          Allow raw writes to the bootloader and partition table area

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>
          Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"

      --probe <SELECTOR>
          Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: human]
          
          [env: POGO_FORMAT=]
          [possible values: human, json, jsonl]

      --config <PATH>
          Config file
          
          [env: POGO_CONFIG=]

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m

      --wait-lock <DURATION>
          Wait for a busy device instead of failing

      --dry-run
          Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing

  -v, --verbose...
          More logs on stderr (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr

      --no-color
          Disable colors

An ELF is converted to an app image and flashed with bootloader and partition table.
A raw .bin requires --address. Writes below the app region need --allow-bootloader-write.
Verifies by default and resets into run mode unless --no-reset.

Examples:
  pogo flash target/riscv32imc-unknown-none-elf/release/app
  pogo flash app.bin --address 0x10000 -d target -f json
  pogo flash app.elf --erase-all --confirm F4:12:FA:9C:3A:10

Exit codes: 0 ok, 3 device not found/ambiguous, 4 timeout, 5 permission denied,
6 device I/O, 8 guardrail refused, 9 device busy

JSON data: { device, chip, flash_size_bytes, regions: [ { address, bytes, kind } ],
verified, reset_after, duration_ms }
